---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReactionNetwork from "../components/ReactionNetwork.astro";
import DigitalLabWorkflow from "../components/DigitalLabWorkflow.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import ResearchArea from "../components/ResearchArea.astro";
import { researchAreas } from "../data/research";
import { technologyGroups } from "../data/projects";
import { organization } from "../data/organization";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Atoms for Humanity | Building a Sustainable Molecular Future"
  description="Atoms for Humanity is a nonprofit research organization building open infrastructure for molecular simulation at massive scale and applying it to sustainable chemistry."
>
  <section class="home-hero">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="hero-wordmark">Atoms for Humanity</p>
        <h1>Building a sustainable molecular future.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Modern civilization is built from molecules. We are developing the scientific capabilities needed to discover and design chemistry for human and environmental health.</p>
        <div class="link-row">
          <a class="button" href="/work">Explore our work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/about">About Atoms for Humanity <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <svg class="hero-texture" viewBox="0 0 1600 900" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice" aria-hidden="true">
      <g class="hero-flow">
        <path class="hero-flow__secondary" d="M-90 345c310 265 585-150 890 66s560 240 895-96" />
        <path class="hero-flow__echo" d="M-130 700c345-190 560 34 790-95s410-405 790-250 345 120 420 75" />
      </g>
    </svg>
    <ul class="container hero-footnote" aria-label="Atoms for Humanity principles">
      <li>MOLECULAR SCIENCE</li><li>OPEN INFRASTRUCTURE</li><li>PUBLIC BENEFIT</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section challenge-section" id="challenge">
    <div class="container split">
      <SectionHeader label="01 — THE CHALLENGE" heading="The chemistry of modern life needs to change." />
      <div class="copy-stack">
        <p>Chemistry underlies our materials, medicines, manufacturing, energy systems, agriculture, and technologies. But many of the molecular systems inherited by modern civilization were optimized for performance and cost without fully accounting for environmental persistence, toxicity, biological compatibility, or long-term sustainability.</p>
        <p>We believe many of these problems can ultimately be addressed at their source: by discovering and designing better chemistry.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--secondary" id="chemical-space">
    <div class="container space-grid">
      <div>
        <SectionHeader label="02 — CHEMICAL SPACE" heading="Finding better chemistry means searching an enormous space." />
        <div class="copy-stack space-copy">
          <p>The spaces of possible molecules, reactions, catalysts, materials, and chemical processes are vast. Traditional experimental discovery can explore only a small fraction of them.</p>
          <p>Increasing humanity's ability to navigate this space is one of the fundamental requirements for building a more sustainable molecular future.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ReactionNetwork />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section why-now" id="why-now">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        label="03 — WHY NOW"
        heading="A new mode of molecular science is becoming possible."
        intro="Molecular simulation provides a way to interrogate physical chemistry computationally. Modern computing provides enormous scale. Artificial intelligence increasingly provides the ability to automate scientific reasoning and exploration. Connecting these capabilities creates the possibility of computational experiments operating at scales that were previously impractical."
      />
      <div class="four-grid">
        <article class="concept"><p class="concept-index">01</p><h3>Simulation</h3><p>Ground scientific questions in molecular physics.</p></article>
        <article class="concept"><p class="concept-index">02</p><h3>Compute</h3><p>Run large numbers of calculations in parallel.</p></article>
        <article class="concept"><p class="concept-index">03</p><h3>AI</h3><p>Automate hypothesis generation, analysis, and scientific iteration.</p></article>
        <article class="concept"><p class="concept-index">04</p><h3>Infrastructure</h3><p>Connect these capabilities into a coherent scientific system.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section laboratory-section" id="digital-laboratory">
    <div class="container laboratory-grid">
      <div class="laboratory-copy">
        <SectionHeader label="04 — THE DIGITAL LABORATORY" heading="A digital chemical laboratory for humans and AI." />
        <div class="copy-stack">
          <p>Atoms for Humanity is building open infrastructure that allows molecular simulations to be constructed, executed, analyzed, and reproduced at massive scale.</p>
          <p>Human researchers can use this environment to investigate chemical systems systematically. AI systems can use the same scientific tools to formulate hypotheses, run computational experiments, interpret results, and decide what to investigate next.</p>
        </div>
        <blockquote>Give increasingly capable AI access to a massively scalable digital chemical laboratory, and it gains something essential: the ability to test ideas against physical models rather than merely propose them.</blockquote>
      </div>
      <DigitalLabWorkflow />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--secondary technology-preview" id="open-infrastructure">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        label="05 — OPEN INFRASTRUCTURE"
        heading="Infrastructure for molecular simulation at scale."
        intro="AFH develops a connected open-source stack spanning scientific data, program interoperability, distributed computation, and cloud access."
      />
      <div class="stack-line" aria-hidden="true"><span>SCIENTIFIC INTENT</span><i></i><span>PHYSICAL COMPUTATION</span></div>
      <div class="technology-groups">
        {technologyGroups.map((project, index) => (
          <article>
            <div class="technology-number">0{index + 1}</div>
            <div>
              <p>{project.category}</p>
              <h3>{project.name}</h3>
              <div class="tech-description">{project.description}</div>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <a class="text-link tech-cta" href="/technology">Explore the technology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section research-section" id="research">
    <div class="container research-grid">
      <div class="research-heading">
        <SectionHeader
          label="06 — RESEARCH"
          heading="Building the tools—and using them to do science."
          intro="Infrastructure matters because of the science it makes possible. AFH develops new computational capabilities alongside an active research program designed to test them against difficult molecular problems."
        />
        <a class="text-link" href="/work">Explore our work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div>
        {researchAreas.map((area) => <ResearchArea area={area} concise />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--light open-science" id="open-science">
    <div class="container open-grid">
      <SectionHeader light label="07 — OPEN SCIENCE" heading="Scientific capabilities should compound." />
      <div>
        <div class="copy-stack">
          <p>We believe the ability to simulate matter at scale should become a scientific public good.</p>
          <p>AFH develops open software, workflows, data, protocols, and scientific results so that researchers beyond our organization can use, extend, and improve what we build.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="open-list">
          <li>Open-source scientific software</li>
          <li>Shared computational infrastructure</li>
          <li>ChemCloud access for external researchers</li>
          <li>Open scientific workflows and data</li>
          <li>AFH Software Fellows</li>
          <li>Scientific collaboration</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="open-note">AFH also provides shared compute and ChemCloud access to external researchers and research groups.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--bright institution-section" id="institution">
    <div class="container institution-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">08 — THE INSTITUTION</p>
        <h2>Building for the long term.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Atoms for Humanity is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit research organization founded to develop scientific capabilities that can serve the public over long timescales.</p>
        <p>AFH's current research and infrastructure program is supported by a <strong>{organization.support.amount} grant from {organization.support.name}</strong>.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/about">About the organization <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .home-hero { position: relative; min-height: calc(100svh - var(--header-height)); display: grid; place-items: center; padding: clamp(6rem, 13vw, 11rem) 0; overflow: hidden; }
  .home-hero::before { position: absolute; inset: 50% auto auto 50%; content: ""; width: min(92vw, 1100px); aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(66,221,177,.07), transparent 64%); transform: translate(-50%, -50%); pointer-events: none; }
  .home-hero::after { position: absolute; inset: 0; content: ""; background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(66,221,177,.024) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(66,221,177,.024) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 80px 80px; mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at center, #000 0, transparent 68%); pointer-events: none; }
  .hero-texture { position: absolute; z-index: 0; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 5%, #000 28%, #000 72%, transparent 96%); }
  .hero-flow { transform-origin: center; animation: hero-flow-drift 22s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
  .hero-flow path { fill: none; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }
  .hero-flow__secondary { stroke: rgba(111,169,184,.085); stroke-width: 1; }
  .hero-flow__echo { stroke: rgba(167,181,175,.06); stroke-width: 1; }
  @keyframes hero-flow-drift { to { transform: translate3d(1.2%, -.6%, 0) scale(1.012); } }
  .hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .hero-copy { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center; }
  .hero-wordmark { margin: 0 0 clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); color: var(--accent); font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 540; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.035em; }
  .hero-copy h1 { max-width: 1220px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 6.8rem); line-height: .98; }
  .hero-lede { max-width: 830px; margin: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem) 0 0; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.5rem); line-height: 1.55; }
  .hero-copy .link-row { justify-content: center; margin-top: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); }
  .hero-footnote { position: absolute; z-index: 1; inset: auto 0 1.4rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-inline: auto; padding: 1.2rem 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-dark); color: var(--text-muted); font: 500 .78rem/1.3 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .1em; list-style: none; }
  .hero-footnote li:nth-child(2) { text-align: center; }
  .hero-footnote li:last-child { text-align: right; }
  .challenge-section { padding-block: clamp(7rem, 14vw, 12rem); }
  .space-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .9fr) minmax(420px, 1.1fr); align-items: center; gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 7rem); }
  .space-copy { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .why-now { background: radial-gradient(circle at 80% 40%, rgba(36,124,104,.07), transparent 30%); }
  .laboratory-section { background: #0d1412; border-block: 1px solid var(--border-dark); }
  .laboratory-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(370px, .85fr); gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem); align-items: center; }
  .laboratory-copy .copy-stack { max-width: 720px; margin-top: 2rem; }
  blockquote { margin: 2.3rem 0 0; padding: .2rem 0 .2rem 1.5rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); color: var(--text-primary); font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.2rem); }
  .stack-line { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 3.5rem; color: var(--text-muted); font: 500 .62rem/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .09em; }
  .stack-line i { height: 1px; flex: 1; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--border-dark), rgba(66,221,177,.4), var(--border-dark)); }
  .technology-groups { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 1rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--border-dark); }
  .technology-groups article { min-height: 360px; display: grid; grid-template-rows: 1fr auto; padding: 1.8rem 1.8rem 2.2rem 0; }
  .technology-groups article + article { padding-left: 1.8rem; border-left: 1px solid var(--border-dark); }
  .technology-number { color: var(--accent); font: 500 .7rem/1 var(--font-mono); }
  .technology-groups p { margin: 0 0 .75rem; color: var(--accent-muted); font: 500 .64rem/1.3 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .technology-groups h3 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font: 520 clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.7rem)/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: -.06em; }
  .tech-description { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .95rem; }
  .tech-cta { margin-top: 2.2rem; }
  .research-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(300px, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 9rem); }
  .research-heading { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--header-height) + 3rem); align-self: start; }
  .research-heading .text-link { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .open-grid, .institution-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 9rem); }
  .open-list { list-style: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); margin: 2.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-light); }
  .open-list li { position: relative; padding: 1rem 1rem 1rem 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light); color: var(--text-dark); font-size: .93rem; }
  .open-list li:nth-child(odd) { padding-left: 0; }
  .open-list li::before { content: "·"; margin-right: .6rem; color: var(--accent-dark); font-weight: 800; }
  .open-note { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; color: var(--text-dark-secondary); font-size: .92rem; }
  .institution-grid h2 { margin: 0; }
  .institution-grid > div:last-child > p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-dark-secondary); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .institution-grid > div:last-child > p + p { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .institution-grid .text-link { margin-top: 1.8rem; }
  @media (max-width: 920px) {
    .home-hero { min-height: calc(100svh - var(--header-height)); }
    .space-grid, .laboratory-grid, .research-grid, .open-grid, .institution-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .space-grid { gap: 2.5rem; }.laboratory-grid { gap: 3rem; }.research-heading { position: static; }
    .technology-groups { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }.technology-groups article { min-height: 240px; }.technology-groups article + article { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-dark); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .home-hero { min-height: auto; padding-block: clamp(5.5rem, 22vw, 8rem); }
    .hero-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(3.3rem, 15vw, 4.5rem); }
    .hero-copy .link-row { flex-direction: column; }
    .hero-footnote { bottom: 1rem; align-items: end; font-size: .64rem; letter-spacing: .055em; }
    .hero-footnote li { max-width: 85px; }
    .hero-footnote li:nth-child(2) { justify-self: center; }
    .hero-footnote li:last-child { justify-self: end; }
    .hero-texture { opacity: .72; }
    .open-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }.open-list li:nth-child(odd), .open-list li { padding-left: 0; }
    .stack-line span { max-width: 92px; }.technology-groups article { min-height: 220px; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .hero-flow { animation: none; } }
</style>
